ock_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the 'warm-to-cold ratio' value (or its exact source of record in ADR 0122) that AC 3's threshold divides by, rather than referencing an unrecorded derived constant.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","F1","T4"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3235,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'holds a p95 below the cold-catch-up p95 divided by the recorded warm-to-cold ratio'","The plan cites ADR 0122's 107 ms local / 545 ms macos figures but never states the 'warm-to-cold ratio' value or where it is recorded; AC 4 only commits to recording the cold-catch-up p95, not the ratio."],"finding":"AC 3's threshold depends on 'the recorded warm-to-cold ratio', a derived constant whose numeric value and source of record are not pinned in the plan.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2d10e1116f0a1253","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, line 3","norm_id":"ne03d344c290a5672","priority":0.4765,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor writing the timing test must divide by a ratio whose value/provenance is unspecified, forcing a clarifying round-trip."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Either define the ratio as a named figure recorded in the ADR 0122 amendments child (same way AC 4 records the cold-catch-up p95), or restate AC 3 to divide by a concrete recorded number.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["docs/adr/0122-similar-ticket-retrieval.md: b505-d66e-86b3-4446 & f10f-c24a-3cfa-449e (no ordering edge)"],"finding":"Sibling tickets touch the same file(s) with no ordering edge.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f82524518cbf636a6","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"na0177dc3af65d74f","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a depends_on/blocks edge to serialize, or partition the file ownership.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["6 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","vague/subjective terms present: better, sufficient"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the failure-disposition contract for the embedding->lexical fallback: label each embedding-tier failure arm (throttle = retryable/transient, auth-denial/parse-empty = fatal/permanent), and state that degrading to the lexical tier preserves the most-recoverable leg by surfacing the retryable embedding throttle in the diagnostic rather than masking it behind the lexical success.","cohort":["T2","T5e","T7","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.failure-disposition-contract"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.834,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'A create succeeds with an empty or lexical-only advisory when the index is absent, when catch-up fails, when the configured embedding provider denies or errors, and when the digest parse yields empty fields.'","'Each of those failure modes emits a diagnostic.'","Default embedding tier is `bedrock:amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0`, whose throttle (429) is a retryable disposition; the plan does not state whether that retryable disposition is preserved or masked by the lexical fallback."],"finding":"The plan adds an embedding-tier -> lexical-tier -> empty-advisory fallback chain ('A create succeeds with an empty or lexical-only advisory when ... the configured embedding provider denies or errors') but never states the disposition contract per arm with an explicit disposition word, nor which disposition wins when the embedding tier fails. The configured default embedding tier is Bedrock Titan; a Bedrock throttle (429) is retryable, yet the plan would silently degrade it to the lexical tier and report create success — the exact 1c0d masking shape (a retryable primary hidden behind a non-retryable/success fallback).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f02aee606b3c4da9d","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — 'A create succeeds with an empty or lexical-only advisory when ... the configured embedding provider denies or errors'","norm_id":"nef9537c36896989f","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Bedrock Titan returns a 429 throttle (retryable/transient): the plan degrades to lexical and reports create success — the diagnostic is emitted but the disposition word is unstated, so a reader cannot tell whether the retryable condition is surfaced anywhere or silently masked.","Embedding provider auth denial (fatal/permanent) vs a transient network error: both collapse to 'degrade to lexical' with no per-arm disposition distinction, so there is no contract saying the fallback preserves the most-recoverable leg."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a 'Failure-disposition contract' note to the Approach (or the embedding-tier child): an embedding throttle stays retryable (surfaced in the diagnostic / counter), an auth-denial or empty-digest-parse is fatal for the embedding tier only; in all cases the create itself is non-blocking and succeeds on the lexical tier, and the diagnostic records the embedding arm's disposition so a retryable throttle is not silently masked by the lexical fallback.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile parent AC3's 'cold-catch-up p95 / warm-to-cold ratio' comparator with 47c8's 'cold rebuild x10' comparator — either align the child's timing test to the cold-catch-up denominator or amend parent AC3 to name the cold-rebuild comparator the child actually enforces.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G3","G4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":"completion","evidence":["Parent AC3: 'Warm-index retrieval holds a p95 below the cold-catch-up p95 divided by the recorded warm-to-cold ratio'","47c8 AC: 'its p95 undercuts the cold rebuild it avoids by at least 10x on the same host ... comparing warm p95 against a same-host cold rebuild'","47c8 ticket comment distinguishes 'cold catch-up p95 12,455 ms' from 'cold full rebuild 16,940 ms' as separate measurements","container pairing: parent + 0461-09ce-4850-42a7/2041-75d6-2a2f-4be9/47c8-97ac-eff3-4e88/80a5-cbb1-ef06-4ba5/b505-d66e-86b3-4446/f10f-c24a-3cfa-449e"],"finding":"Parent acceptance criterion 3 specifies the warm p95 must fall below 'the cold-catch-up p95 divided by the recorded warm-to-cold ratio', but the covering child 47c8 asserts a different comparator: warm p95 must undercut 'the cold rebuild it avoids by at least 10x'. Cold rebuild and cold catch-up are distinct operations in 47c8's own text (its comment reports cold catch-up p95 12,455 ms and cold full rebuild 16,940 ms as separate figures), so the child does not measure the parent criterion in the same terms.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f709e0b81b8ae4c4b","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"child 47c8-97ac-eff3-4e88","norm_id":"n9dd5f2f16a16f7d6","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A completion verifier checking parent AC3 against 47c8's timing test finds the test compares warm p95 to cold REBUILD, not cold CATCH-UP / ratio, so the parent criterion's observable (ratio against cold-catch-up) is never asserted."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Amend parent AC3 to state the comparator 47c8 implements (warm p95 undercuts same-host cold rebuild by WARM_TO_COLD_RATIO), or add a child assertion that also ties warm p95 to the cold-catch-up p95 the parent names.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"insufficient","impact_follows_necessarily":"insufficient","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"insufficient","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"insufficient"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make 47c8's warm/cold-ratio criterion explicitly measure on the same >=10,000-ticket synthetic store its size-precondition criterion asserts, so parent AC3's coupling of ratio-and-size is covered in one place.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":"completion","evidence":["Parent AC3 couples 'a p95 below the cold-catch-up p95 divided by the recorded warm-to-cold ratio, on a synthetic store of at least 10,000 tickets, recomputing zero hashes' into one criterion","47c8 ratio criterion: 'its p95 undercuts the cold rebuild ... over at least 20 runs' (no size named)","47c8 separate criterion: 'That timing test asserts its store holds >= 10,000 tickets before measuring'","container pairing: parent + 0461-09ce-4850-42a7/2041-75d6-2a2f-4be9/47c8-97ac-eff3-4e88/80a5-cbb1-ef06-4ba5/b505-d66e-86b3-4446/f10f-c24a-3cfa-449e"],"finding":"Parent acceptance criterion 3 requires the warm/cold ratio claim to hold 'on a synthetic store of at least 10,000 tickets'. 47c8 splits this across two criteria: the ratio criterion itself only says 'over at least 20 runs ... on the same host' and names no store size, while a SEPARATE 47c8 criterion asserts the timing test's store holds >= 10,000 tickets. The parent couples the size precondition to the ratio claim in one criterion; the child's ratio criterion as worded does not itself bind the >=10,000 precondition, relying on an adjacent criterion to supply it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdb3f15b2e24460c3","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"child 47c8-97ac-eff3-4e88","norm_id":"n133f46e34e03c6c7","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If the two 47c8 criteria were satisfied by tests over different stores, the ratio could be measured on a store smaller than 10,000 while the size assertion passes on a different fixture."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reword 47c8's ratio criterion to read '... over at least 20 runs on the >=10,000-ticket synthetic store it generates' so the size precondition and the ratio claim bind the same fixture.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7143,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"insufficient","impact_follows_necessarily":"insufficient","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"insufficient","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"n